1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,067
Day six. The closed rooms smell like
old air and wet walls. Dust hangs in
the light.

2
00:00:05,767 --> 00:00:09,833
And that's a problem. Asthma. Every
sealed room is a trap for me.

3
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:15,767
Rule five. Air out every closed room
before you walk in. Windows first.
Always.

4
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:21,167
Day seven. You walk to the pharmacy.
You need the one thing you can't live
without.

5
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:27,000
Inhalers. I counted every shelf.
Eleven. Just eleven. For the rest of
my life.

6
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,300
And they expire. Some in a year. Some
in three.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,467
So every puff has a price now. Slow
breathing first. Inhaler last.
